### Key design decisions

| Decision | Reason |
|---|---|
| `process.env` with `??` (nullish coalescing) | Falls back to defaults only when the variable is `undefined` or `null`, not when it is intentionally set to `""`. |
| `parseInt(..., 10)` with explicit radix | Avoids octal/hex surprises and makes the intent clear. |
| Boolean parsed via string comparison | Environment variables are always strings; `=== "true"` is the safest conversion. |
| Validation block | Catches misconfigured environments at startup rather than at the first network call. |
| `Object.freeze` | Prevents other modules from silently mutating shared config state. |

